        <mxCell id="bamgduMelKxRTM5ARuDJ-1" value="Architecture Design Choices:&lt;br&gt;- Both sensors (TSL2591 and&amp;nbsp;AHT20) have online documentation and relevant ressources to easily integrate them inside your applicable, e.g. in python&lt;br&gt;- Python allows to develop very quickly an application, them you can rely on the Oriented Object Programming (OOP) offers by this language to design a very well structure architecture&lt;br&gt;- SQLAlchemy can be easily integrated inside your flask application thanks to its dedicated extension, then it is an Object Relational Mapper (ORM) that allows to define strict relational model (SQL) for which you can declare&amp;nbsp;high-level entities such as classes, objects and methods and use relational query thanks to SQL. In the futur, if needed, you can deploy the application on a dedicated SQL server, for example MySQL or PostgreSQL" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="940" y="160" width="810" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
